{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207294-new-legacy-the-defiant","id":1207294,"title":"[New Legacy] The Defiant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-15T09:10:48-07:00","id":1207294,"title":"[New Legacy] The Defiant","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Sans, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>The Defiance</b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Founding Path:</u> Life/Space (Campaign allows custom paths, Sleepers don\u2019t induce paradox.)<br /> <br /> <u>Ruling Arcanum:</u> Time<br /> <br /> <u>Doctrine:</u> Time 2, Survival 3, and 2 in either Athletics, Stealth, Investigation or Medicine.<br /> They call themselves The Defiance, but are mostly comprised of rangers, trail guides, hunters, and others who spend significant time away from population centres. It attracts rebels, anarchists, the disenfranchised, healers, and others who have a dichotomy within themselves struggling to find their place in society. Taught that the lowest common denominator of a society is the metric to measure it by, they seek to \u2018raise the bar\u2019 and punish what they perceive as corruption or power wholly abused on their path to self mastery and understanding their surroundings. If everyone is one and everywhere is nowhere, true mastery is when the world reaches a perfected state.<br /> <br /> <u>Initiation:</u> Similar to master martial artists and monks, the Guide embarks on a \u201cspirit walk\u201d and must survive in nature for a prolonged period, fasting and studying for a week before their trial \u2013 the period before is often held in natural environments as well, to drive the importance of the <i>whole</i> world being perfected.<br /> <br /> <u>Organization:</u> Among the Rebels and Guides there is a sense of camaraderie and responsibility to the well being of other members but they very rarely gather in any large capacity. Essentially rebels, pilgrims, and roamers. (Once established, any given town or city may have a dozen or less Guides working in small circles of pairs or triplets, organized by whoever is the most experienced.) Often travellers, they\u2019re fairly well connected by word of mouth or beast. Typically they avoid written communication unless security is certain.<br /> <br /> <u>Yantras:</u> Succeeding on a Survival roll relevant to the spell (+2); Aiding the poor (+1, +2 if it\u2019s a significant improvement to their life); Discovering something embarrassing about a member of authority. (+2); Ritualistic Meditation (+2); Breaking out a wrongly accused prisoner or other means of defying the authority (+2); Escaping the authority\u2019s justice (+1, or +2 if the consequences would be severe or there is significant effort towards the capture of the Guide); Unsettled/untamed wilderness (+1)<br /> <br /> <u>Oblations:</u> Meticulously preparing a space (ritualistic circle) and meditating in it. Lecturing on the values of alternatives to linear power structures (Dictatorships, Monarchies, etc). Breaking out a wrongly accused prisoner. Significantly improving the life, providing a sense of purpose, or other largely positive change in the life of someone considered the bottom or excluded from society as a whole. (ie lower class/destitute, the disabled, etc)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attainments:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>First:</b><b> Outlander\u2019s Intuition</b> (Initiation)<br /> When you work against the established authority, it\u2019s only natural you find trouble. Guide\u2019s aren\u2019t afraid to ask hard questions. This attainment mimics the spell \u201cMomentary Flux\u201d cast instantly. The Guide shakes the hands of a new acquaintance for example, and finds reason to investigate.<br /> <b>Optional</b><i>:</i> Space 1<br /> What good is a blind Guide? After a scene spent meditating on their role in the Tapestry and how they can best serve, the guide returns with a broad perspective. This mimics \u201cThe Inward and Outward Eye\u201d with prolonged duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Second:</b><b> Anarch</b><b>ist\u2019s</b><b> Hands</b> (Time 2, Second Skill 3)<br /> Just as they cast their physical senses wide, they keep their temporal wits about them, glimpsing the near future for what wisdom it may hold and taking advantage of it. This mimics \u201cChoose The Thread\u201d cast instantly.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> The Guide knows the land he travels intimately, for if he didn\u2019t, what good would he be to his charges? This mimics \u201cAnalyze Life\u201d with its reach effect, cast instantly.<br /> <br /> <b>T</b><b>hird: </b><b>Healer</b><b>\u2019s </b><b>R</b><b>esolve</b> (Time 3, Survival 4)<br /> When acting against the commonly accepted laws, one needs a contingency plan for getting caught. The Guide may mimic \u201cShifting Sands\u201d cast instantly; commonly used when rounding the corner into authority figures and in need of a fast way out once spotted.<br /> <b>Optional: </b>Space 3<br /> Sometimes it isn\u2019t a second chance you need, it\u2019s space to assess your options. The guide can invert small spaces for short periods, strategically increasing their odds of survival. The Guide may mimic \u201cBan\u201d cast instantly. Some Guides use this to cut an injured ally from the fight, giving them space to rest and recover in the midst of combat. Other Guides use it to cut an enemy out of the fight, in these cases a clash roll scores successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in Space.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth:</b><b> Ranger\u2019s Unguent </b>(Time 4, Survival 5, Second Skill 4, Third Skill 3)<br /> The Guide is more than a bringer of good faith and camaraderie, they can bless themselves or allies. With this attainment they can pick out idealized moments \u2013 granting rote on a number of mundane rolls up to potency. This mimics a Perfecting spell with a primary factor of duration, instantly cast at sensory range and costs a single mana.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 4<br /> Guides often spend long stretches of time away from society and in nature only the fit survive. By progressing this far in the legacy, the Guide has mastered their flesh to live as comfortable as natural denizens of the land do. The mage can mimic \u201cTransform Life\u201d instant cast with advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth: </b><b>Aide\u2019</b><b>s Rebuttal</b> (Time 5, Second Skill 5, Third Skill 4, Fourth Skill 3)<br /> The pinnacle of meditation, a resolute example of self mastery, and a burning idealist. The Guide embodies the downtrodden and their will is his. Inspiring a fervent rush he may bring skills to bear with surprising alacrity \u2013 Mimic \u201cBlink of an Eye\u201d cast instantly.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> Life 5<br /> The Guide has become truly one with the land, and after meditation on their place in the natural order may now mimic \u201cShapeshift\u201d with advanced duration, retaining their mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Drive doc that's being updated likely more regularly than this forum post: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Bt32EmAWFzSr4FHMarDVUlNP6TYv7-2C\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Bt...DVUlNP6TYv7-2C</a>)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-17-2018, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:35:25-07:00","id":1207346,"title":"","content":"Your Legacy looks very good. Its philosophy suggests it would have many Free Councillors and Adamantine Arrows as members.<br /> <br /> However, two of the Attainments drew my attention:<br /> <br /> Acording to my calculations, Constant Presence should have been the second Attainment. Automatic successes in a CoW are already a feature for all Legacies and limiting the effect to the caster would make it even weaker than usual. If, on the other hand, the Attainment is meant to affect not only the caster but also the results of their actions (something which Constant Presence doesn't do by default), that would explain your decision. If you intended the latter, making the Attainment unable to affect others is doubly confusing.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the third Life Attainment feels like it wouldn't find use that often, which could be disappointing for the player. I believe you could copy the Crown of Doctrine from among Seer Prelacies and end up with something conceptually similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T12:27:47-07:00","id":1207367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207294-new-legacy-the-defiant?p=1207346#post1207346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Legacy looks very good. Its philosophy suggests it would have many Free Councillors and Adamantine Arrows as members.<br /> <br /> However, two of the Attainments drew my attention:<br /> <br /> Acording to my calculations, Constant Presence should have been the second Attainment. Automatic successes in a CoW are already a feature for all Legacies and limiting the effect to the caster would make it even weaker than usual. If, on the other hand, the Attainment is meant to affect not only the caster but also the results of their actions (something which Constant Presence doesn't do by default), that would explain your decision. If you intended the latter, making the Attainment unable to affect others is doubly confusing.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the third Life Attainment feels like it wouldn't find use that often, which could be disappointing for the player. I believe you could copy the Crown of Doctrine from among Seer Prelacies and end up with something conceptually similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback. I've actually just finished editing the post with my most recent changes to the Legacy, as I felt it was losing sight of it's goals a bit.<br /> The mage I plan on founding this legacy with was ideally going to be Adamantine Arrow since I could cast magic and do combat actions but we're in a setting where the covenants/orders/major supernatural organizations don't really exist yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-15-2018, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}